{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antiparasitic, Antimalarial", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (52.94%) to An-cecB K=A: 18%, R=L: 12%. GRAVY: -0.309; Mol Wt: 3854.68; mol formula: C181H300N53O39; mol ex coeff: 7040. Activity: inhibited P. falciparum 3D7 (IC50 68.63 uM). In addiiton, it inhibited bacterial growth S.aureus (MIC >200 uM), B. subtilis (MIC 18.94 uM), and E. coli (MIC 12.7 uM). Animal model:mouse: showed a dose-dependent inhibition by 17.03%, 39.35%, and 54.19% when IP treated at 10, 20, and 50 mg/kg (4 hpi), respectively, in P. berghei-infected mice (IP). SAR: An-cecB-2 (seq: RAAKKALPVIAGYKAL) and An-cecB-3 (seq: GKRLEKLGRNVFRAAKK) showed small inhibitory effects at 200 uM, indicating the importance of the N-terminal sequence for peptide activity.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38874346", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antimicrob Agents Chemother. 2024 Jun 14:e0031124. doi: 10.1128/aac.00311-24. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04653", "source_id": "AP04653", "source_numeric_id": "04653", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04653", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antimalarial activity of cecropin antimicrobial peptides derived from Anopheles mosquitoes.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
